From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Auto-close stale sessions and enforce one open session at a
 time

A forgotten session from the morning was still open hours later sitting on
closeout, holding its join code and answering as "the open one" - which is
part of how the class got split across two rows.

src/lib/sessionLifecycle.ts
- closeOtherOpenSessions: starting or adopting a session closes every other
  open row. One class at a time; moving from period 2 to period 3 ends
  period 2 instead of racing it.
- sweepStaleSessions: closes any session that outlived its planned length
  plus a 15 minute grace window. The cutoff is DERIVED from that session's
  own lineup (sequence.steps[].durationSeconds) with a 55 minute floor, not
  a flat clock - a guardrail that can end a class still in progress is worse
  than no guardrail, so the arithmetic only ever errs long. Throttled to one
  real query per minute per instance so /control's 1.2s poll stays cheap.
- Auto-closed sessions clear exactly the fields the teacher-initiated close
  clears, so no projector or Chromebook is left pointing at a dead flow.

Wired into the teacher session GET, session start (forced), and
/api/student/warmup-start, so a stale session is retired by the next request
either surface makes. No cron, nothing to schedule, idempotent.

